Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S08
Scenario title: Meeting Room Reservation
Initial workflow description:
A meeting room is reserved for a team meeting. The organizer checks availability and shares the room information with participants.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What event or condition causes the organizer to start the room reservation process — for example, is it triggered by creating a calendar event, receiving a meeting request, or some other action?",
      "answer": "The process begins when the organizer identifies the need for a meeting and gathers the essential details: when the meeting should occur and how many people will attend. These two pieces of information serve as the starting point that drives the entire booking sequence."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "What system or method does the organizer currently use to check room availability — for instance, a shared calendar, a dedicated booking platform, or a physical sign-up sheet?",
      "answer": "The organizer consults both a scheduling tool and a dedicated space-booking platform to see which rooms are free. These two connected tools together surface what is open at the desired time."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "If the preferred room is not available at the requested time, what steps does the organizer take — do they select an alternative room, propose a different time, or follow an escalation path?",
      "answer": "When no suitable space is free, the scenario flags this as a conflict or unavailability exception. The specific fallback steps — such as choosing a different time or an alternate room — are not explicitly detailed beyond acknowledging that a room-unavailable exception must be handled."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How are participants informed of the confirmed room details — is this done through an automatic calendar invitation, a manual email, a messaging tool, or another channel?",
      "answer": "After securing the room, the organizer updates or creates a scheduling invitation and then separately sends the confirmed location details to all attendees. Both a scheduling tool and a messaging or email platform are used to communicate this information."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "What is the process when a reserved meeting is cancelled or rescheduled — who is responsible for releasing the room, and how is that action carried out?",
      "answer": "Cancellation and rescheduling are listed as exceptions that can arise, but the specific steps for releasing a room or who handles that action are not specified in the available information."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "Is any employee permitted to reserve a meeting room, or are there role-based restrictions or an approval step required before a reservation is confirmed?",
      "answer": "The workflow designates the meeting organizer as the person who performs all booking steps without mentioning an approval layer or role-based restrictions. Any requirement for managerial sign-off or access controls is not specified."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Incorporate the answers and produce an updated structured workflow representation plus automation opportunities.
Record unknown facts as remaining gaps, rather than asserting unsupported details.
